    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0410" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11634: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-15T18:00:00+08:00">December 15, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 15—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>American news correspondent from Nanking reports all Americans [and] other
                    foreigners in city uninjured except German named Sperling whose injury we
                    previously reported. Embassy employees safe and only damage to property suffered
                    by Counselor Peck’s<anchor n="43" xml:id="d495-f1"/> residence which was struck
                    by shrapnel.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Hankow, Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d495-f1" n="43" xml:id="d495-f1-content">
                <p>Willys R. Peck, Counselor of Embassy in China, then at Hankow.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
